---
// UseCases — three columns showing where Codec wins, framed by who's
// at each end of the wire. Pulled from the cross-stack matrix in
// packages/bench/results/2026-05-08T01-15-02Z/MATRIX.md.
//
// The dict-zstd numbers (354 B at 2 K tokens on sglang) are model-to-model
// territory — humans never see the bytes, the dict is pre-shared once,
// and msgpack frames compress to a control byte and a delta.
---

<section id="use-cases" class="section usecases">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">control-plane primitives</p>
    <h2>Three operations. <span class="usecases__title-mute">All on raw token IDs.</span></h2>
    <p class="usecases__lede">
      Codec gives the inference layer the same primitives a service mesh gives
      a microservice fleet: <em>route</em>, <em>dispatch</em>, <em>translate</em>.
      Run them on raw <code>uint32</code> tokens, never on text. The
      compression you see in the receipts below is what falls out for free
      when you stop reserializing every hop.
    </p>

    <div class="usecases__grid">
      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">route</span>
          <h3>Tokens all the way down</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          Models think in tokens. Every middleware in your stack &mdash; gateway, router, log sink &mdash; speaks text, so it detokenizes, JSON-wraps, ships, parses, re-tokenizes &mdash; once per hop, burning CPU and risking KV-cache drift. Codec keeps token IDs as the wire format <em>end-to-end</em>; UTF-8 happens once, at the edge that actually displays text. Same compression options on top (gzip / brotli / dict-zstd). Same framing on every engine; six client languages decode byte-identically.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">16&ndash;1700&times;</span><span>less wire (workload-dep.)</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">3</span><span>engines, one wire</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc uc--m2m">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag uc__tag--accent">dispatch</span>
          <h3>MCP tool calls, leaf-mode bypass</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          The MCP path normally tokenizes the tool result at the gateway, every call. A Codec-aware MCP server
          (<a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/wdunn001/codec-time-leaf" rel="noopener">codec-time-leaf</a>)
          attaches token IDs to its result via
          <code>_meta['ai.codec/leaf-tokenization']</code>; the
          <a href="/docs/codec-metamcp/">codec-metamcp gateway</a> forwards them
          verbatim &mdash; <code>[Codec][leaf]</code> fires, the gateway becomes
          a transparent ID pipe, and the consumer skips its BPE re-tokenize.
          <strong>tools/list</strong> across a 40-tool namespace:
          <strong>21.4&nbsp;KB &rarr; 5.9&nbsp;KB (3.6&times;)</strong>.
          ToolWatcher detects tool boundaries on the raw ID stream at
          <strong>26.7&times;</strong> the speed of detokenize+regex
          (lab EPYC, 481&nbsp;Mtok/s).
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">12.4&times;</span><span>leaf consumer CPU</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">26.7&times;</span><span>ToolWatcher vs detok+regex</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="uc">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag">translate</span>
          <h3>Cross-vocab agent handoff</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          A Llama-3 agent's stream feeds a Qwen-2 agent through one
          in-process detokenize / retokenize step. UTF-8 never crosses
          the wire. At 2&nbsp;K tokens the Codec path ships
          <strong>15.1&times;</strong> fewer wire bytes
          (10.4&nbsp;KB &rarr; 709&nbsp;B) at bridge CPU within noise of
          the JSON-SSE+retokenize path. Both paths emit byte-identical
          Qwen-2 output; the bench asserts strict equality before
          reporting numbers.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">15.1&times;</span><span>smaller wire @ 2K</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">≡</span><span>byte-identical output</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- v0.3 latent modality — VAE latents on the wire. -->
    <div class="usecases__latent">
      <article class="uc uc--latent">
        <header class="uc__head">
          <span class="uc__tag uc__tag--latent">latents</span>
          <h3>Image &amp; video diffusion on the wire</h3>
        </header>
        <p class="uc__body">
          The same wire format extends to <a href="/docs/codec-diffusers/">diffusion
          models</a>: VAE latents stream in length-prefixed binary frames
          instead of decoded pixels. The client runs <code>vae_decode</code>
          locally; pixels never touch the wire. Measured on the lab against
          codec-diffusers running SD-1.5: a 512&times;512 latent at int8 packs
          to <strong>16.4&nbsp;KB</strong> (~5&ndash;10&times; smaller than
          JPEG, ~90&times; smaller than raw fp16 pixels). The int4 pipeline
          halves it again. Pipeline math validates byte-for-byte against
          <a href="https://github.com/wdunn001/Codec/blob/main/spec/PIPELINES.md" rel="noopener">spec/PIPELINES.md</a>.
        </p>
        <ul class="uc__metrics">
          <li><span class="uc__num">3.9&times;</span><span>int4 vs raw latent</span></li>
          <li><span class="uc__num">~90&times;</span><span>vs raw fp16 pixels</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .usecases__title-mute { color: var(--fg-faint); font-weight: 500; }
  .usecases__lede { max-width: 64ch; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .usecases__lede em { color: var(--fg); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }

  .usecases__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .usecases__grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }

  .uc {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .uc--m2m {
    /* model-to-model is the headline use case — give it the accent border */
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 50%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 140% at 0% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 8%, transparent), transparent 65%),
      var(--bg-elev);
  }

  .uc__head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .uc__tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__tag--accent {
    background: var(--data-soft);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--data) 60%, transparent);
    color: var(--data);
  }
  .uc h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .uc__body {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .uc__body strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .uc__body code {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .uc__metrics {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: auto 0 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }
  .uc__metrics li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.125rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .uc__num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--data);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-transform: none;
  }
  .uc--m2m .uc__num { color: var(--control); }

  /* v0.3 latent modality block — sits below the three-column grid as a
     full-width call-out, since the latent pathway is the v0.3 headline
     story and deserves its own visual weight rather than being squeezed
     into a 4th column. */
  .usecases__latent { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .uc--latent {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 50%, var(--border));
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 140% at 100% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent), transparent 65%),
      var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .uc--latent .uc__num { color: var(--accent); }
  .uc__tag--latent {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 18%, transparent);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 60%, transparent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
